From: Felix Li <2524369985@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: Tolerate destination changes during overlay readback.

The composed destination may shrink or become unmapped after its geometry
was sampled. XShmGetImage already traps readback errors, but its XGetImage
fallback used Xlib's fatal default error path. Resizing the companion could
therefore terminate its Media SDK process while the Electron UI survived.

Trap only expected drawable-lifetime/geometry errors for this readback,
keep the current input shape and retry on a later present. Do not change
the image content, capture transport, audio or renderer selection.

Co-Authored-By: OpenAI Codex <noreply@openai.com>

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
@@ -568,6 +568,13 @@
     client_surface_update_offscreen( hwnd, surface );
 }
 
+/* The destination can shrink or become unmapped between geometry and readback. */
+static int overlay_read_error( Display *display, XErrorEvent *event, void *arg )
+{
+    return event->error_code == BadMatch || event->error_code == BadDrawable ||
+           event->error_code == BadWindow;
+}
+
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBXXSHM
 static int overlay_xshm_error( Display *display, XErrorEvent *event, void *arg )
 {
@@ -736,9 +743,17 @@
         }
     }
 #endif
-    if (!image &&
-        !(image = XGetImage( gdi_display, drawable, 0, 0, width, height, AllPlanes, ZPixmap )))
-        return TRUE;
+    if (!image)
+    {
+        X11DRV_expect_error( gdi_display, overlay_read_error, NULL );
+        image = XGetImage( gdi_display, drawable, 0, 0, width, height, AllPlanes, ZPixmap );
+        if (X11DRV_check_error())
+        {
+            if (image) XDestroyImage( image );
+            return TRUE;
+        }
+        if (!image) return TRUE;
+    }
 
     direct = image_is_native_32bpp( image );
 
